From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:22:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0066: textures found once per descriptor

For every texture of every draw, ResolveTexture decoded the descriptor,
computed the image's tiled layout (ImageInfo::UpdateSize) and searched the
texture cache page by page (FindImagesInRegion, SameBacking, the overlap
resolution): 12 % of the command thread in Astro Bot, for bindings that
repeat image after image.

The binding found for a descriptor and a shader resource is kept, with the
texture cache's generation, which grows whenever an image is registered or
freed: as long as it is unchanged, and the image found was alone over its
memory, the same descriptor binds the same image, and only what FindImage
does once it holds the image is repeated (the LRU touch, the materialization
of a pending color clear). Heap descriptors depend on what is mapped and are
resolved every time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
